    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="20" relname="span">According to Dictionary.com, intuitiveness is of, relating to, or arising from intuition; known or perceived through intuition; possessing or demonstrating intuition.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="elaboration">Intuition is knowledge gained by the use of this faculty; a perceptive insight.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="22" relname="span">Another word for intuitiveness is innate knowledge.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="21" relname="span">Innate knowledge is like knowing right from wrong.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="elaboration">You just KNOW that it is wrong to push someone.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="24" relname="circumstance">In regards to program design, when you use it</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="24" relname="span">you should be able to just operate it without having to go through some type of tutorial every time.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="25" relname="span">For example, when you use email.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="27" relname="concession">Even though there are many different user interfaces</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="27" relname="span">it is all the same (generally speaking).</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="10" relname="elaboration">You know that there is going to be a way to reply, forward, delete, view the next email, view the previous email, etc.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="29" relname="solutionhood">How do you measure intuitiveness?</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="29" relname="list">You can measure it by the amount of times that a user has to refer to the Help section after using the system 5 times.</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="30" relname="span">You can test the user on different features of the system.</segment>
        <segment id="15" parent="32" relname="circumstance">For example, when you apply for a job</segment>
        <segment id="16" parent="32" relname="span">and they make you take a test that will see how well you use Microsoft Excel.</segment>
        <segment id="17" parent="16" relname="elaboration">According how many you get wrong will determine how much of an expert you really are.</segment>
        <group id="18" type="multinuc"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="18" relname="joint"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="19" relname="span"/>
